# CodeForChange 2.0 — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is **CodeForChange 2.0**, the official event website for Cloud Native Durgapur's hackathon.
Built with Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19, Tailwind CSS 4, and rich animation libraries.

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router) — `/src/app/`
- **UI**: React 19, Tailwind CSS 4
- **Animations**: Motion (Framer Motion v12), GSAP 3
- **3D/WebGL**: React Three Fiber, React Three Drei, Three.js, OGL
- **Other**: react-snowfall, postprocessing

## Code Style & Conventions

### General
- Use **JavaScript** (not TypeScript) — this project has no TS setup
- Use `"use client"` directive only when the component needs browser APIs or interactivity
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Keep components **small and focused** — one responsibility per file

### File Structure
- App pages go in `src/app/`
- Reusable UI components go in `src/ui/`
- Route-specific components go alongside their page (e.g. `src/app/venue/`)
- Images go in `pictures/` (imported via Next.js Image) or `public/` (for static assets)

### Imports
- Use relative imports (not absolute) — e.g. `../ui/ShinyText`
- Import Next.js `Image` for all `<img>` tags
- Import animations from `motion/react` (not `framer-motion`)

### Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes — avoid inline styles unless for dynamic values
- Use `globals.css` for base styles and CSS variables
- Dark theme by default — keep backgrounds dark, use glassmorphism for cards

### Animations
- Use `motion` from `motion/react` for component animations
- Use GSAP for scroll-triggered or complex timeline animations
- Keep animations smooth — prefer `ease` curves over linear
- Respect reduced motion where possible

### Next.js Specifics
- Always use `next/image` for images with proper `width`/`height` or `fill`
- Use `next/font` if adding fonts
- API routes go in `src/app/api/`
- Use `layout.js` for shared layout, `loading.jsx` for loading states

### Performance
- Lazy load heavy components (3D, WebGL) with `dynamic(() => import(...), { ssr: false })`
- Avoid importing large libraries at the top level if only used in one place
- Use `React.memo` for expensive pure components

## Do NOT
- Add TypeScript — keep `.js`/`.jsx` extensions
- Use `pages/` directory — this is App Router only
- Use `styled-components` or CSS-in-JS
- Commit `node_modules`, `.env`, or `.vercel`
- Break existing animation or 3D component APIs

## CI/CD
- GitHub Actions runs lint (`npx next lint --dir src`) and build on every push/PR
- Vercel auto-deploys on every push to `main`
- Always ensure `npm run build` passes before pushing
